# The Arc tool on the sketch example: a click for the centre, the radius 0.4
# and the start angle 0 typed, a move a quarter turn round and the span 90
# typed draw Arc1; three clicks, the pointer going clockwise between the
# last two, draw Arc2, stored with its ends swapped. Then the Segment tool
# draws L1 from Arc1's end, which it shares as end(Arc1).
open docs/instances/sketch-basic.json
wait 16
action tool.arc
wait 2
click L 724 339
move 789 339 3
wait 2
text "0.4"
key Tab
text "0"
key Enter
wait 2
move 770 293 3
move 724 275 3
wait 2
text "90"
key Enter
wait 2
click L 772 371
click L 805 371
move 795 394 3
move 772 403 3
click L 772 403
wait 2
action tool.segment
wait 2
click L 724 275
click L 660 258
wait 2
key Escape
wait 2
